config MPIPE_AUD
	bool "Audio plugin support"
	select AUDIO
	help
	  Elements that capture, process and play back PCM audio: a digital
	  microphone source, a gain transform, and a sink driving an audio codec
	  over I2S.

	  They sit on Zephyr's audio APIs and describe what they carry as a
	  sample rate, a sample width, a channel count and the layout of those
	  channels within a buffer.

if MPIPE_AUD

config MPIPE_AUD_BUFFER_POOL_SZ_MAX
	int "Size of the largest buffer in the buffer pool"
	default 98304
	help
	  Size in bytes of the largest buffer the audio pool can hand out. It
	  bounds one block of PCM, so it follows from the sample rate, the sample
	  width, the channel count and how much time one buffer covers.

	  The default holds roughly half a second of 48 kHz 16-bit stereo, or a
	  full second of the same in mono. Reserved
	  memory, so lower it when the pipeline's format is known and smaller.

config MPIPE_AUD_BUFFER_POOL_NUM_MAX
	int "Number of maximum sized buffers in the buffer pool"
	default 10
	help
	  Upper bound on how many buffers the audio pool provides. Negotiation
	  settles the number actually used, and this caps what it may ask for.

	  Audio needs more slack than video: a codec starved of data produces an
	  audible artifact rather than a dropped frame, so leave enough for the
	  sink to keep its buffers primed.

config MPIPE_AUD_I2S_CODEC_SINK_SET_OUTPUT_VOLUME
	bool "Set codec output volume in the I2S codec sink"
	help
	  When enabled, the I2S codec sink programs the codec output volume
	  after configuring it. Without this, the codec keeps its driver
	  default (typically 0 dB / unity), which can overdrive the analog
	  output stage and sound distorted on boards with a fixed line/speaker
	  amplifier.

config MPIPE_AUD_I2S_CODEC_SINK_OUTPUT_VOLUME
	int "Codec output volume (codec-specific units)"
	default 106
	depends on MPIPE_AUD_I2S_CODEC_SINK_SET_OUTPUT_VOLUME
	help
	  Output volume value passed to audio_codec_set_property() as the
	  AUDIO_PROPERTY_OUTPUT_VOLUME for AUDIO_CHANNEL_ALL. The units are
	  codec specific. For the WM8962 the field is 7 bits where 121 (0x79)
	  is 0 dB, each step is 1 dB and values up to and including 47 (0x2F)
	  mute the output. The default of 106 is approximately -15 dB.

endif # MPIPE_AUD
